    "summary": "Model now passes all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nRoot cause of the failure: the instance geometry for the precast small-box mid-girder had top-slab thickness t_top written as 0.20 m, whereas the bridge description states \"top slab 0.18 m thick\". The originally accepted girder.single.A/I (1.06052 m², 0.25166 m⁴) were correct for the description, but MR-02's re-integration of the (wrong) stored section gave 1.08635 m² / 0.25476 m⁴, tripping L2-1. The decisions were right; the instance was wrong.\n\nRepair: corrected inst:girder.section.t_top to 0.18 m via write_instance, then re-decided the invalidated section-derived slots per MR-02:\n- girder.single.A = 1.06052 m², girder.single.I = 0.251659 m⁴\n- girder.A = 5 × 1.06052 = 5.30260 m², girder.I = 5 × 0.251659 = 1.258293 m⁴\n- girder.w = 26 × 5.30260 = 137.868 kN/m, girder.m = w/9.81 = 14.0538 t/m\n\nRe-ran modal analysis: f1 = 4.272 Hz (bearing-spring dominated, unchanged), so lane.mu = 0.1767·ln(f1) − 0.0157 = 0.24087 per JTG D60-2015 4.3.2.\n\nFinal model: single simply-supported span, spine-beam 2D idealization; 5 precast prestressed small-box girders (C40, lumped as one equivalent beam) on two abutment lines of 10 plain laminated elastomeric bearings each (spring vertical + longitudinal, free rotation). Results: self-weight reaction 1723.35 kN/ support, self-weight midspan moment 10770.9 kN·m; Class-II lane-load max positive moment 6878.4 kN·m; first vertical bending frequency 4.27 Hz."
